WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.867
A two-dimensional array can be viewed as a grid with rows and columns.

00:00:04.867 --> 00:00:08.682
This structure is similar to a table or matrix.

00:00:08.682 --> 00:00:15.812
In analytics, each row often represents one observation, such as a customer or product,

00:00:15.812 --> 00:00:19.772
while each column represents a numerical variable or measurement.

00:00:20.495 --> 00:00:26.286
For example, we could store products as rows and months as columns.

00:00:26.286 --> 00:00:34.201
Once data is two dimensional, selection and calculation become more powerful, but we also need to pay closer attention

00:00:34.201 --> 00:00:37.106
to shape and axis.

00:00:37.106 --> 00:00:43.636
When you inspect a two-dimensional array, identify how many rows and columns it contains and decide what each direction

00:00:43.636 --> 00:00:47.778
means in the context of the problem.
